! mcp_bootstrap_p227.strap -- MCP printed page 227: the Input Program's
! V EE1 control word, V REOP / V ECP, the V ACT loop and V BLOC block
! count, to V SETUP / V SETX (lines 1-49).
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.234, read at 400 dpi, 1200 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000609  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 227"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224642, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  49 lines, every one located, contiguous from 224642.00 to
! 224672.40 (a half word; next 224673.00).  The volume OCR puts printed
! p.226's last row at 224641.40 (remark -0608) and p.228's line 2 at
! 224673.40 (remark -0655), so the page joins on both sides.  Remarks
! here are DECIMAL sequence numbers -0609 .. -0653; -0648 is not printed
! (line 44 -0647, line 45 -0649).  Lines 10, 15, 18, 22, 40 print none;
! lines 16, 19, 23, 41 print theirs (-0622, -0624, -0627, -0644) one
! field further LEFT than the rest.
!
! >>> CARD SERIALS. <<<  Right-hand serials run ?A000609 .. ?A000653 (the
! prefix glyph is the straight-stemmed round that p.221 read DA; recorded
! as read).  Four pairs share a serial -- lines 15/16 (623), 18/19 (625),
! 22/23 (628), 40/41 (645): each a SIC,(V P) followed by its branch, two
! statements per card, and each pair's second statement is the one whose
! remark prints in the left field.  Asterisks after the LOCATION on
! lines 16 and 39.
!
! >>> LABELS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK. <<<
!  * line 31 prints "V BLCC": at 1200 dpi the third glyph after L is the
!    squared round of this page's VREOP 'O', the fourth the open C.
!    Written VBLOC, the spelling landed p.220 references (BZXVLZ,VBLOC
!    at 224661.40, this row's half word).
!  * line 11 prints "V ECP" with the SAME squared glyph as VREOP's O
!    (line 10, directly above) -- by shape it is very likely V EOP.  It
!    is written VEOP, with the siblings V REOP, V WEOP, V WTEOP and
!    V WFEOP; p.218 line 49's "B,V ECP" (224647.40, this row) is written
!    VEOP the same way.  The bits cannot see the spelling.
!  * line 10 "VREOP" (no space printed after V) -- O by the sibling
!    labels V WTEOP (p.221) and V WEOP (p.218); nothing landed references
!    it, so it rests on ink.
!  * line 30 prints "B,V IC(V U)": written VID, as p.213 line 17 settled
!    the same printed "V IC" (V ID SYN,V NX.V H = 5.32; 000005.50 = 5.40
!    + B's .10).
!  * lines 6/7 V REQ6: the Q's tail is visible at 1200 dpi (Vision reads
!    REG6 on line 6).
!  * line 9 prints "CW,C,O,C" -> CW,0,0,0 (open rounds in a numeric
!    field; binary 000000.00+ 000 000000 000000).
!  * octal-field opens ("CCCCCC.CC", "224671.5C") are 0.

